<TD VALIGN=TOP><A HREF="AATHierarchy?find=&logic=&note=&page=1&subjectid=300138708"><IMG SRC="/global/images/global_hierarchy.gif" WIDTH=13 HEIGHT=14 BORDER=0></A></TD>
<TD COLSPAN=4 VALIGN=BOTTOM><SPAN CLASS=page><B>fashion design</B> (design (discipline), arts-related disciplines, ... Disciplines (hierarchy name))</SPAN></TD></TR>
<TR><TD><P>&nbsp;</P></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD COLSPAN=5><SPAN CLASS=page><B>Note: </B>Designing clothing, accessories, and ensembles for personal wear. For the design of clothing, accessories, and ensembles intended to create an appearance characteristic of a particular period, person, place, or thing, especially (but not exclusively) for theatrical performances, use "costume design."  For the concept of a prevailing, usually short lived custom, usage, or style in clothing, cars, restaurants, and other personal possessions and services, use "fashion."<BR>&nbsp;</SPAN></TD></TR>
<TR>
<TD COLSPAN=3><SPAN CLASS=page><B>Terms:</B></SPAN></TD></TR>
